<setup>

  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="-0.2" to="0.2" step="0.1" exclude="0"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="h" from="-2" to="2" exclude="0"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="-2" to="2" exclude="0"/>

  <math name="signa"><sign>$a</sign></math>
  <math name="yPoint" simplify>$k - $signa*2</math>

  <function name="f">$a*(x-$h)^2+$k</function>

  <derivative name="df">$f</derivative>

  <function name="fp" through="$A $B $C" styleNumber="3" />

  <point name="A" styleNumber="2">(-3,4)
      <attractTo name="c1">$df</attractTo>
  </point>

  <point name="B" styleNumber="2">(0,4)
      <attractTo name="c2">$df</attractTo>
  </point>

  <point name="C" styleNumber="2">(3,4)
      <attractTo name="c3">$df</attractTo>
  </point>
</setup>

<p>
  Sketch an approximate graph of the derivative of the given quadratic function <m>f(x)</m>.  To do so, drag the red points so that they lie on the graph of <m>f'(x)</m> in such a way that it makes the orange curve be the graph of <m>f'(x)</m>.
</p>

<graph grid="true" fixAxes="true" showNavigation="false" fixAxes="true" xMin="-6" xMax="6" yMin="-6" yMax="6">
  <shortDescription>A parabola and a curve through three movable points, which should be dragged so that the curve is the derivative of the parabola</shortDescription>
  $f
    <label anchor="(2,$$f(2)-0.5)"><m>f</m></label>
  $A
  $B
  $C
  $fp
</graph>

<p>
  One way to accomplish this is to identify any <m>x</m>-values where <m>f'(x) \approx 0</m>, and then identify any <m>x</m>-values where <m>f'(x) \approx \pm 1</m> and drag the red points to the corresponding locations.
</p>

<answer><award><when>
   $A.constraintUsed and $B.constraintUsed and $C.constraintUsed
</when></award></answer>
